Subject: [PATCH 01/13] C16, patch 1 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M22; a
 cold reader's finding (a) on R80b's part 2, patch 11, NOT CHECKED BY MAIN,
 MADE AGAIN BEFORE IT WAS MENDED): IN B1895'S CARRIER CHECK, ONE CORRECTION
 EXCUSES ONLY THE OLD WORDS IT FOLLOWS

THE FINDING, MADE AGAIN. In a verdict file, each place of the old words was given a window that ran 400
characters past it, and a correction anywhere in the window excused it. So two old phrases with one correction
after both were both excused: a planted line "A: <old>. B: <other old> [<correction>]." gave (0 uncorrected, 2
places) on the lock as it stood.

THE MEND. A window ends where the next place of old words begins, so a correction excuses the words it follows
and no earlier ones. The lines as they stood are kept in a dated note in the function.

THE TEST, added to the lock: the plant is now (1, 2); its twin, each old phrase with its own correction, is
(0, 2); the same old phrase twice with one correction after the second is (1, 2); B1881's verdict file, which
this arc names, reads as before. The lock: 13 passed. Not checked by main.
